                <mxCell id="62" value="FPGA Internal Easy to design&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Host System CPU Loading &amp;lt; XDMA&lt;/div&gt;" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;backgroundOutline=1;darkOpacity=0.05;" vertex="1" parent="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="320" y="790" width="240" height="100" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="63" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Google Sans Text&amp;quot;; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;&quot;&gt;QDMA&#39;s architectural design, especially its ability to stream data directly to the FPGA logic and manage numerous queues efficiently, drastically reduces the CPU&#39;s role in data movement compared to XDMA, making it&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: &amp;quot;Google Sans Text&amp;quot;; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 21px; color: rgb(51, 51, 255);&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt; far superior for high-throughput, low-latency applications by offloading significant work to the FPGA&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Google Sans Text&amp;quot;; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;&quot;&gt;. &lt;/span&gt;" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;backgroundOutline=1;darkOpacity=0.05;strokeColor=default;fontColor=default;" vertex="1" parent="1">
